def pairs_2025():
    o = [chapter_open("NAMES 20 TO 25 — TOGETHER", "الْقَابِضُ الْبَاسِطُ · الْخَافِضُ الرَّافِعُ · الْمُعِزُّ الْمُذِلُّ", "The Names That Come in Pairs",
                      "Al-Qabid & Al-Basit · Al-Khafid & Ar-Rafi' · Al-Mu'izz & Al-Mudhill", None)]
    o.append(h2("1. Why These Names Come in Pairs"))
    o.append(p("Most of the Names of Allah can be said on their own. These six go in pairs. A single one, heard alone, could give a wrong impression, as if Allah only takes, only lowers, only humbles. The Prophet ﷺ himself said them together: *\"Indeed Allah is the One who sets prices, the One who constricts, the One who expands, the Provider\"* (Sunan Abi Dawud 3451). And many scholars point out that these Names should be used together, so that the full meaning is clear: He has complete power over both, and He uses each with perfect wisdom."))
    o.append(box("He gives and withholds · He raises and lowers · He honours and humbles — always in wisdom, never in cruelty, never in randomness."))
    o.append(h2("2. The Three Pairs"))
    o.append(table(["Pair", "The two sides", "Seen in"], [
        ["Al-Qabid · Al-Basit", "Constricts · Expands. Provision, ease, and even the heart itself.", "Qur'an 2:245; 13:26; 17:30"],
        ["Al-Khafid · Ar-Rafi'", "Lowers · Raises. Ranks, stations and the Day of Judgement.", "Qur'an 56:3; 58:11"],
        ["Al-Mu'izz · Al-Mudhill", "Honours · Humbles. Who truly holds honour and who loses it.", "Qur'an 3:26; 22:18"]]))
    o.append(h2("3. A Test of Reading Correctly"))
    o.append(ayah_box(ayah(89, 15, 16)))
    o.append(p("This is perhaps the most important ayah for understanding these pairs. A person is given wealth and says, *my Lord has honoured me.* The same person is constricted and says, *my Lord has humiliated me.* And the very next ayah answers both with one word:"))
    o.append(ayah_box({"ar": ["كَلَّا"], "en": "\"No!\" (Qur'an 89:17)", "ref": ""}))
    o.append(p("No. Neither expansion nor constriction is the measure of your worth with Allah. Both are tests. The person who is given much is asked how he thanks; the person who is given little is asked how he is patient. The true raising and the true lowering are decided by something else entirely: taqwa. As the Qur'an says, *\"the most noble of you in the sight of Allah is the most righteous of you\"* (49:13)."))
    o.append(h2("4. What Each Pair Teaches"))
    o.append(h3("Al-Qabid and Al-Basit: your provision and your heart"))
    o.append(p("They teach that wealth and ease are not signs of being loved, and tightness is not a sign of being forsaken. Both are from the same wise hand, and both are meant to bring you back to Him.", "note"))
    o.append(h3("Al-Khafid and Ar-Rafi': your rank"))
    o.append(p("They teach that rank, as the world gives it, is not the same as rank with Allah. The one who lowers himself before Him is raised; the one who raises himself above Him is lowered.", "note"))
    o.append(h3("Al-Mu'izz and Al-Mudhill: your honour"))
    o.append(p("They teach where honour truly comes from. *\"Whoever desires honour, then to Allah belongs all honour\"* (35:10). It is never taken by force and it is never given by the crowd. It is given by Him, and withdrawn by Him, in justice.", "note"))
    o.append(h2("5. Essence Together"))
    o.append(essence("Allah holds every opposite in His hand: He gives and withholds, raises and lowers, honours and humbles. In all of it He is wise, and in all of it He is Just, so that the believer is steady in ease and in hardship, since both are His and both are His care."))
    o.append(h2("6. For You, the Servant"))
    o.append(p("In every season of your life, ask yourself which side of the pair you are standing on, and what Allah is asking of you there. If you are in expansion, the question is *gratitude and generosity*. If you are in constriction, the question is *patience and trust*. If you feel raised, the question is *humility*. If you feel lowered, the question is *return*. In both, He is near."))
    o.append(chapter_close())
    return "\n".join(o)


